WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.080
The more I read about it,
the more I investigated,

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.850
the more I began to realize that,

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.033
oh my God, this is a huge story

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.420
and it raised so many obvious questions

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.850
about culture within these institutions

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.180
that I was just hooked

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.223
and I've been following it ever since.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.440
Next to a landmark ruling

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.480
on what's been called the
biggest tax heist ever,

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.530
Germany's top criminal court

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:30.320
has outlawed the
controversial trading practice

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.230
known as Cum-Ex.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:37.230
In short, it was the
world's biggest banks,

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:42.750
brokerages, lawyers,
accountants, hedge funds,

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.170
coming together over a decade

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:49.060
to make billions and billions of dollars

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.460
at the direct expense of
taxpayers across Europe.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.730
How much did you make
from cum dividend trading?

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.200
How much did you make?

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.310
I think it was in the
region of 700 million,

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.350
but it's hard to put a figure on it

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.963
because of currency exchanges and so on.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.260
Sanjay Shah is basically a trader

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:12.050
who has become the poster
boy for that scandal.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:15.980
It's hard to think of
too many other traders

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:18.010
in the history of the city

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:22.300
who have become so rich in
such a short space of time.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.240
So at the moment,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.790
my financial situation
is everything is frozen

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:28.880
and I'm allowed money to live on.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.620
So the court in the UK

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.820
has approved for me to get paid
every month living expenses

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.763
and also my legal fees and that's it.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:52.050
So Sanjay grew up in London
in the '70s and '80s.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.800
London-born, London-raised,
son of a doctor,

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.650
went to medical school
himself, dropped out.

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:03.100
He first started off
working at Merrill Lynch

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.950
and then Morgan Stanley
in the back offices.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.640
I think he found it quite mundane.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:08.950
He very much was desperate

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.533
to get on the trading
floor, in the action.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.900
Every morning, I used
to turn up to the office

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.410
and see a row of sports
cars parked outside

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:21.240
and I said to my boss,
"Who drives these cars?"

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.950
And he said, "The traders
do on the fifth floor."

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.580
So I then decided that I wanted
to be one of those people.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.630
And he eventually landed
on the trading floor

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:30.760
at Credit Suisse,

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.190
which was where he first learned

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.160
about dividend arbitrage trading.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.560
He began to observe these
quite complex trades

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:44.560
that exploited taxes on dividends
in a really lucrative way.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.990
Now, what he told us was

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:49.910
while you're doing various kinds of trades

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:53.320
trying to profit from dividend
taxes up to that point,

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.030
the first time he started
doing Cum-Ex trades

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:59.520
was at Rabobank on the eve
of the financial crisis

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.583
around 2007, 2008.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.420
I think to understand Cum-Ex,

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.140
you kind of have to go back to London

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.450
in the early 2000s,

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:14.030
which was when traders in
the city began to figure out

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:15.760
how they could profit

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.470
from something that's
called a withholding tax.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.800
These traders would make

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.250
what is known as withholding
tax applications.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:28.690
So they would make claims for tax refunds

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:33.420
multiple times on dividend
taxes that they only paid once.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:35.150
Analogies for this that I've read

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.823
are like it's the equivalent of saying,

00:03:38.992 --> 00:03:40.950
you know, me, you

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.680
and a few other people were
entitled to tax refunds

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.530
because we all made a donation to charity

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:51.210
whereas in reality, it was
just me who made that donation.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.490
But through a series

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:55.930
of kind of very complicated
rapid transactions,

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:59.940
we concealed or we made
it very difficult to tell

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.810
exactly who it was

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.970
that made that donation on
the date that it was made.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:08.600
So they hand out the tax
relief to a number of parties.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.420
That's what Cum-Ex is

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.330
except that it doesn't take
place with charitable donations,

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:16.453
it takes place with taxes on dividends.

00:04:18.864 --> 00:04:19.930
This is gonna be one of the watershed days

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.560
in the financial market's histories.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.060
The day began with a bailout,

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.520
the prime minister and the
chancellor making it clear

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.540
that the financial system is
so important to our society

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:29.950
that by saving our banks,

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.303
we're saving ourselves.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.960
During the financial crisis, however,

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:38.050
Rabobank decided to stop doing Cum-Ex

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:40.730
and dividend tax kinds of transactions.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:44.220
So Sanjay was out of a job once again.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.180
And he decided in 2009

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.380
instead of finding more work at a bank,

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.170
that he would set up his own hedge fund.

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.310
I didn't want to be

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.330
someone who is trying
to get a job in a bank

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:58.060
when no banks were hiring.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:02.130
I think he very much
wanted to reap more awards

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:04.960
from the trading floor than
what a bank would allow.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.460
So he set up his own fund

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:09.030
and called it Solo Capital Partners

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:10.780
to reflect that desire

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.730
to keep all the profits for himself.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.790
He started his fund in 2009

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.220
with just half a million pounds,

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.970
which really wasn't much at all.

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:22.530
But this trading strategy
was so profitable

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:25.830
that he amassed a fortune
of several times that.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.800
Within three or four years,

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.960
he had turned that into a personal fortune

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.940
of about $700 million.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:37.210
And for about six years,
he lived the high life.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:39.410
He was making hundreds
of millions of pounds

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.210
as were his employees

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.973
and he eventually went over to Dubai.

00:05:46.344 --> 00:05:51.003
And he used that fortune
to buy a 32 foot yacht.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.880
He then traded that in
for a 62 foot yacht.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:58.350
He bought property in Hong Kong.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.670
He bought property in London.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.130
He bought property in New
York, property in Dubai,

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.730
where he was now based.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:07.480
He amassed this global property portfolio

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:11.070
and he amassed this huge personal fortune.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.290
I was advised don't leave Dubai

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:14.350
because you will be arrested

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.160
and you'll be put in pretrial detention.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:17.730
In 2016,

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:22.650
after Sanjay had made hundreds
of millions of dollars,

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.690
Solo Capital Partners shut down.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:27.380
Around this time,

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:31.700
investigations into Cum-Ex
trades were swirling,

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.870
not just around Sanjay and Solo,

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:36.560
but around the industry in general.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:39.400
The Cum-Ex tax fraud scheme,

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.470
this has been mentioned
has cost EU countries,

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:47.070
a reported €55 billion,
a huge sum of money,

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:50.800
to complex share deals
with no economic purpose

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:54.740
other than to receive tax
reimbursements from the state

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.960
and no actual tax being paid.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:01.960
European citizens have, to
put it bluntly, been robbed.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:06.090
Cum-Ex, it was always an aggressive,

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:09.300
controversial trading strategy,

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.455
but what people in the industry say

00:07:11.455 --> 00:07:16.100
is that Sanjay Shah and Solo
Capital went even further.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.690
He's accused by prosecutors

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:21.110
of creating this network
of global entities,

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:23.830
including small U.S. pension funds,

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:27.420
and in one case a Jewish
school in New York

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:32.040
to claim refunds on taxes
on behalf of them as well.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:34.080
So in terms of the Jewish school,

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.630
that one really was audacious.

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:37.930
The German prosecutors

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.320
say he claimed to represent this school,

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.180
which had tax exempt status

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.690
because of their religious status

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:46.680
in this agreement between
Germany and the U.S.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:50.790
So he claimed that they
would buy German shares

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:52.990
and then his fund on behalf of them

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.410
would claim these refunds on those taxes

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.900
apparently without their knowledge.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.093
What German prosecutors allege

00:08:01.093 --> 00:08:06.093
is that Sanjay used
this small Jewish school

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:09.380
and its tax exempt status

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:14.380
to pull off about $1.1 billion of trades.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:19.340
This presumably delivers
huge profits to Sanjay

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:20.940
and his hedge fund Solo Capital.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.350
Sanjay is now facing a legal assault

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.200
on multiple fronts, okay?

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:31.500
He's got the Danish criminal charges

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.110
which have been pressed against him.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:37.860
Then more recently,
prosecutors in Hamburg, Germany

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:41.480
have also pressed criminal
charges against Sanjay.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:44.313
You feel that you you're
being targeted individually?

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.330
Yeah, I feel I'm being targeted

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.100
and one of the reasons why

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:50.820
is that right from the beginning

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:53.500
the Danish authorities
accused me of fraud.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:54.640
Being accused of fraud

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:59.100
means assets can be frozen by
prosecutors around the world.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:02.020
It puts a label to me, which is unfair

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.978
and after five years,
nothing has been proven.

00:09:03.978 --> 00:09:05.020
There's two things.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:08.060
There was the legality of
this and the morality of this.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.520
And for Denmark,

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:12.150
they say that Sanjay masterminded

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.800
a two billion dollar fraud
against their country,

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.380
and that's nearly one
percent of their GDP.

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:20.710
And so the morality of this

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:24.980
at a time when a country is
reeling from financial crisis

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:27.270
and there's mass unemployment

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:31.000
and state funding is being
squeezed across Europe,

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.400
to defraud a small economy like that

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:36.708
out of two billion dollars

00:09:36.708 --> 00:09:40.150
is really quite something.

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:45.010
When we pushed him on the,
I guess the morals of this,

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:50.010
he said himself that bankers
and traders have no morals.

00:09:50.232 --> 00:09:51.690
The only thing that matters

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.267
is whether you make money legally or not.

00:09:53.267 --> 00:09:55.337
"All I was doing", he says,

00:09:55.337 --> 00:09:58.180
"was exploiting that arbitrage

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.190
the same way that traders have done

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:02.940
down through the decades, nothing new."

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:04.650
Well, yeah, the barn doors were open.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:07.070
They were told the barn doors were open.

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:09.860
People were driving trucks into the barn

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:13.780
taking out truckloads of cash for decades

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:17.366
and it's their bad.

00:10:17.366 --> 00:10:19.470
There was an opportunity to be had.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.670
I'm not the only one who
took the opportunity.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:23.150
There are many others.

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:25.800
So it's really important to remember

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:30.800
that even if Sanjay is the poster boy

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:33.650
of the Cum-Ex scandal,

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.980
he's a product of an industry,

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.380
he isn't the industry by himself.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.520
This was not a rogue trading strategy

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:45.350
that Sanjay dreamed up
in his flat in London.

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:46.910
This was a trading strategy

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:49.650
that as we've reported and
as others have reported

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:52.310
was signed off at the highest levels

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:55.790
of some of the world's biggest
financial institutions.

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:57.120
Cum-Ex investigations

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:58.940
have really taken off in the past year.

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:02.430
Germany now has around 1,000 suspects.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.650
They've convicted three former bankers.

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:07.460
They've charged around a dozen others.

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:10.145
Three trials are currently underway

00:11:10.145 --> 00:11:11.360
and it's really spread

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:13.500
to some of the biggest
institutions in Europe.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.242
I don't know where to
start with Deutsche Bank.

00:11:15.242 --> 00:11:18.260
As Alex said, they had a
downgrade at the end of last week.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:20.820
There are reports that
Garth Richie and Mr. Jane,

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:23.680
the former CEO under investigation
now for this tax problem.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.250
So for example, at Deutsche Bank,

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:29.400
80 current and former employees
are being investigated.

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.710
Deutsche Bank has specifically said

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:34.040
that it never directly participated

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:37.170
as a short seller or a
buyer in Cum-Ex deals

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:40.210
and it is cooperating with authorities

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:43.540
and in Denmark where Sanjay
Shah is under investigation,

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:45.350
things have moved more slowly.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:48.390
He and others have now been charged.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:49.320
But as far as we know,

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:51.490
nothing has been done to
try and extradite them.

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:52.800
He remains in Dubai

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:55.930
where it's very hard to
extradite individuals,

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:58.300
but this isn't the end of the story

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.070
when it comes to Cum-Ex investigations,

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.580
really we really are
right at the beginning.

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:04.840
I got to tell you that when I'm,

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:06.800
I believe I'm gonna be clear of this soon,

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:08.200
maybe in a year or two.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.250
When I am, I will be back in business

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.773
and I will be pursuing
these types of trades.

